#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kurso ng IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuits"
msgstr "Mga Circuit"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In computer science, *circuits* are models of computation in which information is carried by wires through a network of *gates*, which represent operations on the information carried by the wires.\n"
"*Quantum circuits* are a specific model of computation based on this more general concept.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa computer science, ang mga *circuit* ay mga modelo ng computation kung saan dinadala ng mga wire ang impormasyon sa pamamagitan ng isang network ng mga *gate*, na kumakatawan sa mga operasyon sa impormasyong dinadala ng mga wire.\n"
"Ang *quantum circuits* ay isang espesipikong modelo ng computation na nakabatay sa mas pangkalahatang konsepto na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although the word \"circuit\" often refers to a circular path, circular paths aren't actually allowed in the circuit models of computation that are most commonly studied.\n"
"That is to say, we usually consider *acyclic circuits* when we're thinking about circuits as computational models.\n"
"Quantum circuits follow this pattern; a quantum circuit represents a finite sequence of operations that cannot contain feedback loops.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit na ang salitang \"circuit\" ay madalas na tumutukoy sa isang pabilog na landas, hindi talaga pinapayagan ang mga pabilog na landas sa mga modelo ng circuit ng computation na pinag-aaralan nang madalas.\n"
"Sa madaling salita, karaniwang isinasaalang-alang natin ang mga *acyclic circuit* kapag iniisip natin ang mga circuit bilang mga modelo ng computation.\n"
"Sumusunod ang mga quantum circuit sa pattern na ito; ang isang quantum circuit ay kumakatawan sa isang limitadong pagkakasunud-sunod ng mga operasyon na hindi makakapaglaman ng mga feedback loop.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boolean circuits {#boolean-circuits}"
msgstr "Mga Boolean circuit {#boolean-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is an example of a (classical) Boolean circuit, where the wires carry binary values and the gates represent Boolean logic operations:\n"
msgstr "Narito ang isang halimbawa ng isang (klasikal) na Boolean circuit, kung saan ang mga wire ay nagdadala ng mga binary value at ang mga gate ay kumakatawan sa mga operasyon ng Boolean logic:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Example of a Boolean circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-XOR.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Halimbawa ng isang Boolean circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-XOR.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The flow of information along the wires goes from left to right: the wires on the left-hand side of the figure labeled $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are input bits, which can each be set to whatever binary value we choose, and the wire on the right-hand side is the output.\n"
"The intermediate wires take whatever values are determined by the gates, which are evaluated from left to right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang daloy ng impormasyon sa kahabaan ng mga wire ay mula kaliwa hanggang kanan: ang mga wire sa kaliwang bahagi ng figure na may label na $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay mga input bit, na maaaring itakda sa anumang binary value na ating napili, at ang wire sa kanang bahagi ay ang output.\n"
"Ang mga intermediate na wire ay kumukuha ng anumang value na tinutukoy ng mga gate, na sinusuri mula kaliwa hanggang kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The gates are AND gates (labeled $\\wedge$), OR gates (labeled $\\vee$), and NOT gates (labeled $\\neg$).\n"
"The functions computed by these gates will likely be familiar to many readers, but here they are represented by tables of values:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga gate ay AND gates (may label na $\\wedge$), OR gates (may label na $\\vee$), at NOT gates (may label na $\\neg$).\n"
"Ang mga function na kinakalkula ng mga gate na ito ay malamang na pamilyar sa maraming mambabasa, ngunit narito ang mga ito na kinakatawan ng mga talahanayan ng mga value:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & \\neg a\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\wedge b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 0\\\\\n"
"  10 & 0\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\vee b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  a & \\neg a\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  0 & 1\\\\\n"
"  1 & 0\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\wedge b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 0\\\\\n"
"  10 & 0\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\qquad\\quad\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\vee b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 1\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The two small, solid circles on the wires just to the right of the names $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ represent *fan-out* operations, which simply create a copy of whatever value is carried on the wire on which they appear, allowing this value to be input into multiple gates.\n"
"Fan-out operations are not always considered to be gates in the classical setting; sometimes they're treated as if they're \"free\" in some sense.\n"
"When Boolean circuits are converted into equivalent quantum circuits, however, we do need to classify fan-out operations explicitly as gates to handle and account for them correctly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dalawang maliit na solidong bilog sa mga wire na nasa kanan lamang ng mga pangalan na $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay kumakatawan sa mga operasyong *fan-out*, na simpleng gumagawa ng kopya ng anumang value na dinadala sa wire kung saan ito lumabas, na nagbibigay-daan sa value na ito na ma-input sa maraming gate.\n"
"Ang mga operasyong fan-out ay hindi laging itinuturing na mga gate sa klasikal na setting; minsan ay tinatrato sila na parang \"libre\" sa ilang paraan.\n"
"Kapag ang mga Boolean circuit ay na-convert sa katumbas na mga quantum circuit, gayunpaman, kailangan nating malinaw na uriin ang mga operasyong fan-out bilang mga gate upang mahawakan at maipaliwanag ang mga ito nang tama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here's the same circuit illustrated in a style more common in electrical engineering, which uses conventional symbols for the AND, OR, and NOT gates:\n"
msgstr "Narito ang parehong circuit na inilalarawan sa isang estilo na mas karaniwan sa electrical engineering, na gumagamit ng mga kumbensyonal na simbolo para sa AND, OR, at NOT gate:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Boolean circuit in a classic style](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-classic.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Boolean circuit sa klasikong estilo](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/Boolean-circuit-classic.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We won't use this style or these particular gate symbols further, but we will use different symbols to represent gates in quantum circuits, which we'll explain as we encounter them.\n"
msgstr "Hindi natin gagamitin ang estilo na ito o ang mga partikular na simbolo ng gate na ito pa, ngunit gagamit tayo ng iba't ibang simbolo upang kumatawan sa mga gate sa mga quantum circuit, na ipapaliwanag natin habang nakakatagpo tayo ng mga ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The particular circuit in this example computes the *exclusive-OR* (or XOR for short), which is denoted by the symbol $\\oplus$:\n"
msgstr "Ang partikular na circuit sa halimbawang ito ay nagkalkula ng *exclusive-OR* (o XOR nang maigsi), na tinutukoy ng simbolo na $\\oplus$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\oplus b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{c|c}\n"
"  ab & a \\oplus b\\\\\n"
"  \\hline\n"
"  00 & 0\\\\\n"
"  01 & 1\\\\\n"
"  10 & 1\\\\\n"
"  11 & 0\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next diagram we consider just one choice for the inputs: $\\mathsf{X}=0$ and $\\mathsf{Y}=1$.\n"
"Each wire is labeled by value it carries so you can follow the operations.\n"
"The output value is $1$ in this case, which is the correct value for the XOR: $0 \\oplus 1 = 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa susunod na diagram, isinasaalang-alang natin ang isang pagpipilian para sa mga input: $\\mathsf{X}=0$ at $\\mathsf{Y}=1.$\n"
"Ang bawat wire ay may label na value na dala nito upang masubaybayan mo ang mga operasyon.\n"
"Ang output value ay $1$ sa kasong ito, na siyang tamang value para sa XOR: $0 \\oplus 1 = 1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Evaluating a Boolean circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/XOR-circuit-evaluate.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Pagsusuri ng isang Boolean circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/XOR-circuit-evaluate.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The other three possible input settings can be checked in a similar way.\n"
msgstr "Ang tatlong ibang posibleng setting ng input ay maaaring suriin sa katulad na paraan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other types of circuits {#other-types-of-circuits}"
msgstr "Iba pang uri ng mga circuit {#other-types-of-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As was suggested above, the notion of a circuit in computer science is very general.\n"
"For example, circuits whose wires carry values other than $0$ and $1$ are sometimes analyzed, as are gates representing different choices of operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng iminumungkahi sa itaas, ang konsepto ng isang circuit sa computer science ay napaka-pangkalahatan.\n"
"Halimbawa, minsan ay sinusuri ang mga circuit na ang mga wire ay nagdadala ng mga value maliban sa $0$ at $1$, gayundin ang mga gate na kumakatawan sa iba't ibang pagpipilian ng mga operasyon.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In *arithmetic circuits*, for instance, the wires may carry integer values while the gates represent arithmetic operations, such as addition and multiplication.\n"
"The following figure depicts an arithmetic circuit that takes two variable input values ($x$ and $y$) as well as a third input set to the value $1$.\n"
"The values carried by the wires, as functions of the values $x$ and $y$, are shown in the figure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga *arithmetic circuit*, halimbawa, ang mga wire ay maaaring magdala ng mga integer value habang ang mga gate ay kumakatawan sa mga arithmetic na operasyon, tulad ng addition at multiplication.\n"
"Ang sumusunod na figure ay naglalarawan ng isang arithmetic circuit na kumukuha ng dalawang variable na input value ($x$ at $y$) pati na rin ang isang ikatlong input na nakatakda sa value na $1$.\n"
"Ang mga value na dinadala ng mga wire, bilang mga function ng mga value na $x$ at $y$, ay ipinapakita sa figure.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Example arithmetic circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/arithmetic-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Halimbawa ng arithmetic circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/arithmetic-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also consider circuits that incorporate randomness, such as ones where gates represent probabilistic operations.\n"
msgstr "Maaari rin tayong isaalang-alang ang mga circuit na nagsasama ng randomness, tulad ng mga circuit kung saan ang mga gate ay kumakatawan sa mga probabilistikong operasyon.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum circuits {#quantum-circuits}"
msgstr "Mga quantum circuit {#quantum-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the quantum circuit model, wires represent qubits and gates represent operations on these qubits.\n"
"We'll focus for now on operations we've encountered so far, namely *unitary operations* and *standard basis measurements*.\n"
"As we learn about other sorts of quantum operations and measurements, we can enhance our model accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa quantum circuit model, ang mga wire ay kumakatawan sa mga qubit at ang mga gate ay kumakatawan sa mga operasyon sa mga qubit na ito.\n"
"Magtutuon muna tayo sa mga operasyong natagpuan natin sa ngayon, lalo na ang mga *unitary operation* at *standard basis measurement*.\n"
"Habang natututo tayo tungkol sa iba pang uri ng mga quantum operation at measurement, maaari nating palawakin ang ating modelo nang naaayon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here's a simple example of a quantum circuit:\n"
msgstr "Narito ang isang simpleng halimbawa ng isang quantum circuit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Simple quantum circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Simpleng quantum circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this circuit, we have a single qubit named $\\mathsf{X}$, which is represented by the horizontal line, and a sequence of gates representing unitary operations on this qubit.\n"
"Just like in the examples above, the flow of information goes from left to right — so the first operation performed is a Hadamard operation, the second is an $S$ operation, the third is another Hadamard operation, and the final operation is a $T$ operation.\n"
"Applying the entire circuit therefore applies the composition of these operations, $T H S H$, to the qubit $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa circuit na ito, mayroon tayong iisang qubit na pinangalanang $\\mathsf{X},$ na kinakatawan ng pahalang na linya, at isang pagkakasunud-sunod ng mga gate na kumakatawan sa mga unitary operation sa qubit na ito.\n"
"Tulad ng sa mga halimbawa sa itaas, ang daloy ng impormasyon ay mula kaliwa hanggang kanan — kaya ang unang operasyong isinasagawa ay isang Hadamard operation, ang pangalawa ay isang $S$ operation, ang pangatlo ay isa pang Hadamard operation, at ang huling operasyon ay isang $T$ operation.\n"
"Ang pag-apply ng buong circuit ay nag-a-apply ng komposisyon ng mga operasyong ito, $T H S H,$ sa qubit na $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sometimes we may wish to explicitly indicate the input or output states of circuits.\n"
"For example, if we apply the operation $T H S H$ to the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$, we obtain the state\n"
"$\\frac{1+i}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle$. This can be indicated as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Minsan ay nais nating malinaw na ipahiwatig ang mga input o output state ng mga circuit.\n"
"Halimbawa, kung ia-apply natin ang operasyong $T H S H$ sa state na $\\vert 0\\rangle$, makukuha natin ang state na\n"
"$\\frac{1+i}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle$. Maaari itong ipahiwatig tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Simple quantum circuit evaluated](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit-evaluated.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Simpleng quantum circuit na sinuri](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/simple-quantum-circuit-evaluated.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits often start out with all qubits initialized to $\\vert 0\\rangle$, as we have in this case, but there are also situations where the input qubits are initially set to different states.\n"
"Here's another example of a quantum circuit, this time with two qubits:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum circuit ay madalas na nagsisimula sa lahat ng qubit na na-initialize sa $\\vert 0\\rangle$, tulad ng mayroon tayo sa kasong ito, ngunit mayroon ding mga sitwasyon kung saan ang mga input qubit ay unang itinakda sa iba't ibang state.\n"
"Narito ang isa pang halimbawa ng isang quantum circuit, sa pagkakataong ito na may dalawang qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Quantum circuit that creates an e-bit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Quantum circuit na lumilikha ng e-bit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As always, the gate labeled $H$ refers to a Hadamard operation, while the second gate is a *controlled-NOT* operation: the solid circle represents the *control qubit* and the circle resembling the symbol $\\oplus$ denotes the *target qubit.*\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng palagi, ang gate na may label na $H$ ay tumutukoy sa isang Hadamard operation, habang ang pangalawang gate ay isang operasyong *controlled-NOT*: ang solidong bilog ay kumakatawan sa *control qubit* at ang bilog na kahawig ng simbolo na $\\oplus$ ay nagtatanda ng *target qubit.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before examining this circuit in greater detail and explaining what it does, it is imperative that we first clarify how qubits are ordered in quantum circuits.\n"
"This connects with the convention that Qiskit uses for naming and ordering systems that was mentioned briefly in the previous lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago suriin ang circuit na ito nang mas detalyado at ipaliwanag kung ano ang ginagawa nito, napakahalaga na una nating linawin kung paano ino-order (inaayos ang pagkakasunud-sunod ng) ang mga qubit sa mga quantum circuit.\n"
"Ito ay konektado sa kombensyon na ginagamit ng Qiskit para sa pagpapangalan at pag-oorder ng mga sistema na binanggit nang maigsi sa nakaraang aralin.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Qiskit's qubit ordering convention for circuits\">\n"
"In Qiskit, the *topmost* qubit in a circuit diagram has index $0$ and corresponds to the *rightmost* position in a tuple of qubits (or in a string, Cartesian product, or tensor product corresponding to this tuple), the *second-from-top* qubit has index $1$, and corresponds to the position *second-from-right* in a tuple, and so on. The *bottommost* qubit, which has the highest index, therefore corresponds to the *leftmost* position in a tuple. In particular, Qiskit's default names for the qubits in an $n$-qubit circuit are represented by the $n$-tuple $(\\mathsf{q_{n-1}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{0}})$, with $\\mathsf{q_{0}}$ being the qubit on the top and $\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ on the bottom in quantum circuit diagrams.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Kombensyon ng Qiskit sa pag-oorder ng qubit para sa mga circuit\">\n"
"Sa Qiskit, ang *pinakamataas* na qubit sa isang circuit diagram ay may index na $0$ at tumutugma sa *pinakakanang* posisyon sa isang tuple ng mga qubit (o sa isang string, Cartesian product, o tensor product na tumutugma sa tuple na ito), ang *pangalawa mula sa itaas* na qubit ay may index na $1$, at tumutugma sa posisyon na *pangalawa mula sa kanan* sa isang tuple, at iba pa. Ang *pinakamababang* qubit, na may pinakamataas na index, ay samakatuwid ay tumutugma sa *pinakakaliwang* posisyon sa isang tuple. Sa partikular, ang mga default na pangalan ng Qiskit para sa mga qubit sa isang $n$-qubit na circuit ay kinakatawan ng $n$-tuple na $(\\mathsf{q_{n-1}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{0}})$, na may $\\mathsf{q_{0}}$ bilang qubit sa itaas at $\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ sa ibaba sa mga quantum circuit diagram.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is a reversal of a more common convention for ordering qubits in circuits, and is a frequent source of confusion.\n"
"Further information on this ordering convention can be found on the [Bit-ordering in Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering) documentation page.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ito ay isang pagbabago ng isang mas karaniwang kombensyon para sa pag-oorder ng mga qubit sa mga circuit, at isang madalas na pinagmumulan ng kalituhan.\n"
"Ang karagdagang impormasyon sa kombensyon ng pag-oorder na ito ay makikita sa pahina ng dokumentasyon ng [Bit-ordering sa Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although we sometimes deviate from the specific default names $\\mathsf{q_{0}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ used for qubits by Qiskit, we will always follow the ordering convention described above when interpreting circuit diagrams throughout this course.\n"
"Thus, our interpretation of the circuit above is that it describes an operation on a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"If the input to the circuit is a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\phi\\rangle$, for instance, then this means that the lower qubit $\\mathsf{X}$ starts in the state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and the upper qubit $\\mathsf{Y}$ starts in the state $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit na minsan ay lumilihis tayo mula sa mga partikular na default na pangalan na $\\mathsf{q_{0}},\\ldots,\\mathsf{q_{n-1}}$ na ginagamit para sa mga qubit ng Qiskit, lagi nating susundin ang kombensyon ng pag-oorder na inilarawan sa itaas kapag binibigyang-kahulugan ang mga circuit diagram sa buong kursong ito.\n"
"Kaya, ang aming interpretasyon ng circuit sa itaas ay naglalarawan ito ng isang operasyon sa isang pares ng mga qubit na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Kung ang input sa circuit ay isang quantum state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\phi\\rangle$, halimbawa, nangangahulugan ito na ang mas mababang qubit na $\\mathsf{X}$ ay nagsisimula sa state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ at ang mas mataas na qubit na $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay nagsisimula sa state na $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To understand what the circuit does, we can go from left to right through its operations.\n"
msgstr "Upang maunawaan kung ano ang ginagawa ng circuit, maaari tayong lumakad mula kaliwa hanggang kanan sa pamamagitan ng mga operasyon nito.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first operation is a Hadamard operation on $\\mathsf{Y}$:\n"
msgstr "Ang unang operasyon ay isang Hadamard operation sa $\\mathsf{Y}$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   ![First operation e-bit creator](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-first.svg)\n"
msgstr "   ![Unang operasyon ng e-bit creator](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-first.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   When applying a gate to a single qubit like this, nothing happens to the other qubits (which is just one other qubit in this case). Nothing happening is equivalent to the identity operation being performed. The dotted rectangle in the figure above therefore represents this operation:\n"
msgstr "   Kapag nag-a-apply ng gate sa iisang qubit tulad nito, walang nangyayari sa iba pang mga qubit (na isang qubit lamang ang iba sa kasong ito). Ang walang nangyayari ay katumbas ng pagsasagawa ng identity operation. Ang naka-dotted na rektanggulo sa figure sa itaas ay samakatuwid ay kumakatawan sa operasyong ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\mathbb{I}\\otimes H\n"
"     = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\mathbb{I}\\otimes H\n"
"     = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Note that the identity matrix is on the left of the tensor product and $H$ is on the right, which is consistent with Qiskit's ordering convention.\n"
msgstr "   Tandaan na ang identity matrix ay nasa kaliwa ng tensor product at ang $H$ ay nasa kanan, na naaayon sa kombensyon ng pag-oorder ng Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second operation is the controlled-NOT operation, where $\\mathsf{Y}$ is the control and $\\mathsf{X}$ is the target:\n"
msgstr "Ang pangalawang operasyon ay ang controlled-NOT operation, kung saan ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ang control at ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ang target:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   ![Second operation e-bit creator](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-second.svg)\n"
msgstr "   ![Pangalawang operasyon ng e-bit creator](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-second.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   The controlled-NOT gate's action on standard basis states is as follows:\n"
msgstr "   Ang aksyon ng controlled-NOT gate sa mga standard basis state ay ang sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   ![Controlled-NOT gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/cNOT.svg)\n"
msgstr "   ![Controlled-NOT gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/cNOT.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Given that we order the qubits as $(\\mathsf{X}, \\mathsf{Y})$, with $\\mathsf{X}$ being on the bottom and $\\mathsf{Y}$ being on the top of our circuit, the matrix representation of the controlled-NOT gate is this:\n"
msgstr "   Dahil ino-order natin ang mga qubit bilang $(\\mathsf{X}, \\mathsf{Y})$, na may $\\mathsf{X}$ sa ibaba at $\\mathsf{Y}$ sa itaas ng ating circuit, ang matrix representation ng controlled-NOT gate ay ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"     \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"     1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"     0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"     \\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unitary operation implemented by the entire circuit, which we'll give the name $U$, is the composition of the operations:\n"
msgstr "Ang unitary operation na isinasagawa ng buong circuit, na bibigyan natin ng pangalang $U$, ay ang komposisyon ng mga operasyon:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 1 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, recalling our notation for the Bell states,\n"
msgstr "Sa partikular, na alaalahanin ang ating notasyon para sa mga Bell state,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 0 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 1 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 1 \\rangle\n"
"                         - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 0 \\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "we find that\n"
msgstr "nalaman natin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U \\vert 00\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 01\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 10\\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 11\\rangle & = -\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U \\vert 00\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 01\\rangle & = \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 10\\rangle & = \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\\\\n"
"U \\vert 11\\rangle & = -\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This circuit therefore gives us a way to create the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ if we run it on two qubits initialized to $\\vert 00\\rangle$.\n"
"More generally, it provides us with a way to convert the standard basis to the Bell basis.\n"
"(Note that, while it is not important for this example, the $-1$ phase factor on the last state, $-\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle$, could be eliminated if we wanted by making a small addition to the circuit.\n"
"For instance, we could add a controlled-$Z$ gate at the beginning, which is similar to a controlled-NOT gate except that a $Z$ operation is applied to the target qubit rather than a NOT operation when the control is set to $1$.\n"
"Alternatively, we could add a swap gate at the end. Either choice eliminates the minus sign without affecting the circuit's action on the other three standard basis states.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang circuit na ito ay nagbibigay sa atin ng paraan upang likhain ang state na $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ kung patakbuhin natin ito sa dalawang qubit na na-initialize sa $\\vert 00\\rangle.$\n"
"Sa mas pangkalahatang paraan, nagbibigay ito sa atin ng paraan upang i-convert ang standard basis sa Bell basis.\n"
"(Tandaan na, kahit na hindi ito mahalaga para sa halimbawang ito, ang $-1$ phase factor sa huling state, $-\\vert \\psi^-\\rangle,$ ay maaaring alisin kung gusto natin sa pamamagitan ng paggawa ng maliit na karagdagan sa circuit.\n"
"Halimbawa, maaari tayong magdagdag ng isang controlled-$Z$ gate sa simula, na katulad ng isang controlled-NOT gate maliban na ang isang $Z$ operation ay ina-apply sa target qubit kaysa sa isang NOT operation kapag ang control ay nakatakda sa $1.$\n"
"Bilang alternatibo, maaari tayong magdagdag ng isang swap gate sa dulo. Ang alinman sa pagpipilian ay nag-aalis ng minus sign nang hindi naaapektuhan ang aksyon ng circuit sa tatlong iba pang standard basis state.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, quantum circuits can contain any number of qubit wires. We may also include *classical bit* wires, which are indicated by double lines, like in this example:\n"
msgstr "Sa pangkalahatan, ang mga quantum circuit ay maaaring maglaman ng anumang bilang ng mga qubit wire. Maaari rin tayong magsama ng mga *classical bit* wire, na ipinahiwatig ng mga double line, tulad ng sa halimbawang ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Example circuit with measurements](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Halimbawang circuit na may mga measurement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured.svg)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we have a Hadamard gate and a controlled-NOT gate on two qubits $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$, just like in the previous example.\n"
"We also have two *classical* bits, $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$, as well as two measurement gates.\n"
"The measurement gates represent standard basis measurements:\n"
"the qubits are changed into their post-measurement states, while the measurement outcomes are *overwritten* onto the classical bits to which the arrows point.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito mayroon tayong isang Hadamard gate at isang controlled-NOT gate sa dalawang qubit na $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y},$ tulad ng sa nakaraang halimbawa.\n"
"Mayroon din tayong dalawang *klasikal* na bit, $\\mathsf{A}$ at $\\mathsf{B},$ pati na rin ang dalawang measurement gate.\n"
"Ang mga measurement gate ay kumakatawan sa mga standard basis measurement:\n"
"ang mga qubit ay binabago sa kanilang mga post-measurement state, habang ang mga resulta ng measurement ay *na-overwrite* sa mga klasikal na bit na tinuturo ng mga arrow.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's often convenient to depict a measurement as a gate that takes a qubit as input and outputs a classical bit (as opposed to outputting the qubit in its post-measurement state and writing the result to a separate classical bit).\n"
"This means the measured qubit has been discarded and can safely be ignored thereafter, its state having changed into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ or $\\vert 1\\rangle$ depending upon the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Madalas na maginhawa na ilalarawan ang isang measurement bilang isang gate na kumukuha ng qubit bilang input at nag-o-output ng isang klasikal na bit (kumpara sa pag-output ng qubit sa post-measurement state nito at pagsulat ng resulta sa isang hiwalay na klasikal na bit).\n"
"Nangangahulugan ito na ang nasukat na qubit ay itinapon na at maaaring ligtas na balewalain pagkatapon nito, ang state nito ay nagbago sa $\\vert 0\\rangle$ o $\\vert 1\\rangle$ depende sa resulta ng measurement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, the following circuit diagram represents the same process as the one in the previous diagram, but where we disregard $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ after measuring them:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa, ang sumusunod na circuit diagram ay kumakatawan sa parehong proseso tulad ng sa nakaraang diagram, ngunit kung saan binabalewala natin ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ pagkatapos sukatin ang mga ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Example circuit with measurements compact](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured-compact.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Halimbawang circuit na may mga measurement (compact)](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/ebit-circuit-measured-compact.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the course continues, we'll see more examples of quantum circuits, which are usually more complicated than the simple examples above.\n"
"Here are some examples of symbols used to denote gates that commonly appear in circuit diagrams:\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang nagpapatuloy ang kurso, makakakita tayo ng mas maraming halimbawa ng mga quantum circuit, na karaniwang mas kumplikado kaysa sa mga simpleng halimbawa sa itaas.\n"
"Narito ang ilang halimbawa ng mga simbolo na ginagamit upang tukuyin ang mga gate na karaniwang lumalabas sa mga circuit diagram:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Single-qubit gates are generally shown as squares with a letter indicating which operation it is, like this:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga single-qubit gate ay karaniwang ipinapakita bilang mga parisukat na may titik na nagpapahiwatig kung anong operasyon ito, tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ![Single-qubit gates](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/single-qubit-gates.svg)\n"
msgstr "  ![Mga single-qubit gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/single-qubit-gates.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Not gates (or equivalently, $X$ gates) are also sometimes denoted by a circle around a plus sign:\n"
msgstr "  Ang mga Not gate (o katumbas nito, ang mga $X$ gate) ay minsan din tinutukoy ng isang bilog na may plus sign sa loob:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ![Not gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/not-gate.svg)\n"
msgstr "  ![Not gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/not-gate.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Swap gates are denoted as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga swap gate ay tinutukoy tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ![Swap gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/swap-gate.svg)\n"
msgstr "  ![Swap gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/swap-gate.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Controlled-gates, meaning gates that describe controlled-unitary operations, are denoted by a\n"
"filled-in circle (indicating the control) connected by a vertical line to whatever operation is being controlled. For instance, controlled-NOT gates, controlled-controlled-NOT (or Toffoli) gates, and controlled-swap (Fredkin) gates are denoted like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga controlled-gate, na ibig sabihin ay mga gate na naglalarawan ng mga controlled-unitary operation, ay tinutukoy ng isang\n"
"punung bilog (na nagpapahiwatig ng control) na konektado ng patayong linya sa anumang operasyong kinokontrol. Halimbawa, ang mga controlled-NOT gate, controlled-controlled-NOT (o Toffoli) gate, at controlled-swap (Fredkin) gate ay tinutukoy tulad nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ![Controlled gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/controlled-gates.svg)\n"
msgstr "  ![Controlled gate](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/controlled-gates.svg)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arbitrary unitary operations on multiple qubits may be viewed as gates. They are depicted by rectangles labeled by the name of the unitary operation. For instance, here is a depiction of an (unspecified) unitary operation $U$ as a gate, along with a controlled version of this gate:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga arbitrary na unitary operation sa maraming qubit ay maaaring tingnan bilang mga gate. Sila ay inilalarawan ng mga rektanggulo na may label na pangalan ng unitary operation. Halimbawa, narito ang isang paglalarawan ng isang (hindi tinukoy) na unitary operation na $U$ bilang isang gate, kasama ang isang controlled na bersyon ng gate na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ![Arbitrary unitary gate together with controlled version](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/uncontrolled-and-controlled-unitary.svg)\n"
msgstr "  ![Arbitrary unitary gate kasama ang controlled na bersyon](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/uncontrolled-and-controlled-unitary.svg)\n"
